#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:103
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Create the folio repository with `bun run cat init-folio` (or the folio_init tool): content/, the document, chapter and first block manifests, the builder shim, AGENTS.md, .mcp.json, the session-start hook and the beans store, with the platform linked rather than copied."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:111
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every block edit runs the HCI validation gate — see editing-hci-validation.bpmn."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:76
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Gateway_ReviewOutcome sits in this lane rather than a separate editor's, so in this diagram the reviewer's finding and its disposition are the same decision — iterate back to Task_AuthorBlocks or clear Task_Publish — because paper authoring has no editor lane to hold the accept/reject split modelled elsewhere in this corpus."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:120
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Give each formal block (definition, theorem, lemma, proposition, corollary, conjecture, proof) a .lean sibling that Lean 4 accepts, in the order lean-formalization sets out. A compiling declaration is not a formalised claim: check vacuity and narrative drift before calling it done, and record the status with proof-verification."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:208
#. Diagram label
msgid "green"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:27
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "How a scientific paper or book folio is authored end to end, with Lean for its formal claims and LaTeX for its typesetting. folio-assistant — authoring a scientific paper end to end (Lean + LaTeX). Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG. The <bootstrap.processes:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill that implements it; <cat-harness.processes:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared work plan in beans/."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:212
#. Diagram label
msgid "iterate"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:67
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Its three tasks bracket the human review rather than replace it: Validate and Render turn the Lean-green manuscript into the artefact Task_Review actually reads, and Publish only fires once Gateway_ReviewOutcome has said 'approved' — this lane builds what gets judged and executes what was decided, and decides nothing itself."
msgstr ""

