msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:191
#. Diagram label
msgid "Not yours — left alone"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:179
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the bean"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:61
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owns its own loop: Gateway_LeanGreen's 'not yet' branch returns straight to Task_Formalize rather than out to a person, and the gateway itself is DMN-computed off the build result rather than argued, so nothing downstream can proceed on a proof that merely looks close enough. The paper does not reach Task_Validate until this lane's own gate says green."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:176
#. Diagram label
msgid "Paper published"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:196
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:180
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:186
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:162
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ready to publish?"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:155
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Review the rendered paper, not a description of it, and record the feedback. The outcome is iterate — back to authoring — or approved for the publication path."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:75
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reviewer / SME"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:139
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Run content validation over the folio: schemas, the content profile (formal kinds only in a paper), cross-block consistency and that the Lean builds. Loop back rather than rendering over a failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Scaffolds the repo from the author's plan and then writes every block — including every revision, since Gateway_ReviewOutcome's 'iterate' branch re-enters Task_AuthorBlocks directly rather than sending the change back to Lane_Author to be re-scoped. The plan is the author's decision; executing against it, first draft through every rewrite, is this lane's."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:86
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Scope the paper: chapters, the blocks each needs, what gets formalised."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:169
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "See draft-to-publication.bpmn for the review and release path this expands into."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:47
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Sits between Task_Plan and Task_Scaffold as the one conversion point in this diagram: the author's plan becomes beans here, which is what lets a resumed session or a different agent pick up Task_Scaffold without having sat through Task_Plan itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:192
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:94
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The plan becomes beans, so a resumed session or a sibling agent can pick it up."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:41
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The plan set here — chapters, the blocks each needs, what gets formalised — is upstream of everything else in the diagram and is never revisited: Gateway_ReviewOutcome's 'iterate' branch re-enters Lane_Agent's Task_AuthorBlocks directly, not this lane, so a scoping mistake made here surfaces only as churn several lanes downstream."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:163
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer's call after step 8. `iterate` returns to authoring with the feedback; `approved` goes to publish."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:147
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Typeset the paper through LaTeX to PDF and HTML. Run latex_preflight first — missing packages, fonts or engine — rather than discovering them twenty minutes in. The preamble, class and macros belong to the folio, never to the platform."
msgstr ""

